{% doc %}
  Calls the host app's MCP bridge, the one seam between the desk and
  pos-module-mcp.

  The desk cannot reference modules/mcp itself: the MCP module is optional (a
  devDependency), so a desk without it would get missing-partial errors at lint
  time and a 500 at run time, and this module may only reference the modules in
  tests/ci-static.sh. The host app implements hook_support_mcp instead and
  delegates there.

  A desk with no implementation gets nil from every action, which is how the
  Agents and Approvals pages know the integration is absent and stay hidden
  rather than failing.
  @param {string} action - available | tools | agents | connect | revoke | set_tools
  @param {object} [payload] - action arguments, merged into the hook params
  @return {object|null} the hook's answer, or null when nothing implements it
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  assign params = {}
  if payload
    assign params = params | hash_merge: payload
  endif
  assign params['action'] = action
  function results = 'modules/core/commands/hook/fire', hook: 'support_mcp', params: params, merge_to_object: false
  assign answer = results.first
  return answer
%}
